{"data":{"body":"**[P3] Update the documented flush cadence**\n\nThe new invocation-end path calls `drain()` for every sampled-in invocation, and the tests assert that an invocation emitting no record still starts the worker and flushes once. This note still says such invocations do neither. Document that only sampled-out invocations skip flushing; sampled-in invocation ends always flush.","comment_node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPsIIsM7xWkH2","finding_digest":"141e3c093d73aa544e53e1e48405ef30ed779d0643db4dd069368e095b8114d5","finding_id":"arf_v1_cqpdycj5oovfitst4hsiibppgd","finding_key":"insight/readme.md::asynchronous-export-note::flush-cadence","identity_key":"insight/readme.md::asynchronous-export-note::flush-cadence","line":225,"observation_digest":"e23da1ef60babd3eaad8cfe7d9ebf96d4ac7ec91984af35e5d785a8be4809895","observation_id":"aro_v1_4i62d33axk6t5kwyz7t5t27znv","path":"packages/aws-durable-execution-sdk-python-insight/README.md","prior_finding_id":"","published_at":"2026-09-18T17:43:49Z","review_id":"arr_v1_6fhf2wx7p6nkoh4vhu54b3irhz","reviewed_base_sha":"d3230f34a0dbba856b39787b6b568de03de89123","reviewed_head_sha":"717ef06d47ee2badd14806bf7126bc08d4fc7848","reviewer":"codex","start_line":224,"suggestion_id":""},"pull_request":{"number":737},"record_id":"art_v1_gqascdg6vkfxu3r3mun4qdfilw","record_type":"finding_observed","recorded_at":"2026-09-18T17:43:49Z","repository":{"full_name":"aws/aws-durable-execution-sdk-python","id":1052903600},"schema_version":1}
